// demos/mcplay/main.fi -- playable prototype: joins a Minecraft server (offline mode), opens a window, renders the streamed world
// and lets you walk / fly, break and place blocks.
//
//   mcplay <host> <port> <name>   (host = DNS name or IPv4; names resolve over IPv6 and IPv4)
//
// Controls: mouse look (captured), W A S D, Space (jump / up), Shift (sneak / down), Ctrl (sprint), 1-9 / wheel (hotbar),
// LMB break (creative: instant, otherwise hold MCPLAY_DIG_MS), RMB place, F fly on/off, N noclip, F11 fullscreen, Esc release the
// mouse (click captures again), Alt+F4 / window close quits.
//
// Environment (all optional):
//   MCPLAY_GL=1        GL path: glwindow (EGL/GLX) + gl_mc/gl_scene back end, frame shown without read back; MCPLAY_VSYNC=0|1 (default 1); default on Windows (falls back to Vulkan, then CPU); CPU elsewhere
//   MCPLAY_GFX=vk      Vulkan back end (mc.vk_mc: sky, world, entities, tint, HUD in one render pass, frame read back and shown through the X11 window); default = CPU raster.
//                      lavapipe (CPU Vulkan) when there is no GPU. MCPLAY_VK_CACHE=<file> pipeline cache file; MCPLAY_VK_LOST_AT=<frame> simulates a device loss (tests)
//   MCPLAY_EDGE_EXP=0  CPU raster: exact top-left fill rule (no edge expansion, default 1 = on). Reference for GL / Vulkan picture comparisons (r261)
//   MCPLAY_SHOT_SETTLE=1  the MCPLAY_SHOT picture is taken after a stream flush also with LOD (LOD builds + cross-fades done): reproducible picture (r265; CPU vs CPU was 32 dB without)
//   MCPLAY_FACECULL=1  GL: opaque meshes sorted by face direction, a section draws only directions facing the camera (same image; 0 = off)
//   MCPLAY_VIEW=6      view distance in chunks            MCPLAY_PROTOCOL=763   protocol number
//   MCPLAY_LOD=<n>     LOD terrain beyond MCPLAY_VIEW up to n chunks (mc_stream + mc_lod, cross-fade at ring changes; asks the server for n chunks); 0 = off. Default: MCPLAY_VIEW > 8 draws 8 chunks in full detail and LOD up to MCPLAY_VIEW
//   MCPLAY_MODELS=1    (default: auto = on whenever resource packs are loaded, also with MCPLAY_LOD (models only in the full-detail ring, the LOD rings stay cubes), on every back end (CPU / GL / Vulkan); 0 = off) resource pack models (blockstates + models of the packs, mc_model_mesh): stairs, slabs, plants ... are drawn from their baked quads instead of
//                      full cubes. Needs packs (MC_PACKS ...); works on the CPU, GL (MCPLAY_GL=1) and Vulkan (MCPLAY_GFX=vk) back ends; works with mc_stream (worker meshing, MCPLAY_STREAM=1, default) and with MCPLAY_STREAM=0; no LOD; the T key reloads the models too.
//   MCPLAY_PICK_PROBE="ox,oy,oz,dx,dy,dz[;...]"  pick rays (thousandths) at the end of the run, printed as `mcplay: probe ...` (tests; with MCPLAY_MODELS=1 through mc_model_pick)
//   MCPLAY_STREAM=0    old path: mc_render_world (inline meshing) instead of mc_stream. DEFAULT is mc_stream (frustum + cave culling, worker meshing)
//   MCPLAY_WORKERS=N   mesher threads of the stream (0 = inline on the render thread); default clamp(cores - 2, 2, 12) on every path incl. MCPLAY_GFX=vk
//   MCPLAY_W / MCPLAY_H window size (default 854x480)     MCPLAY_FULLSCREEN=1   start fullscreen
//   MCPLAY_FPS=N       frame cap override (0 = uncapped; default = Max Framerate option)   MCPLAY_VSYNC=0|1  vsync override (default = VSync option; GL swap interval / Vulkan FIFO vs IMMEDIATE)
//   MCPLAY_CREATIVE=1  the server is creative: fly allowed and the creative reach (6 blocks)
//   MCPLAY_POS_REPLY=1  old behaviour: answer a server teleport with Teleport Confirm + an immediate move (rubber band storm under load, r197; for A/B runs)
//   MCPLAY_AUTOJUMP=1  Auto-Jump (vanilla option, default off): walking against a 1 block step jumps by itself
//   MCPLAY_POS_LOG=1  every 5th tick one `poslog` line (tick, tp count, pos in mm, vy, ground, fly)
//   MCPLAY_TICKS=2000  time of day until the first update_time packet arrives (then the server time drives the sky)
//   MCPLAY_LIGHT=1     vertex light (mc_wlight: Chunk.light + 5x5 column region, edits repair it) + sky daylight uniform; 0 = old flat tint
//   log:   MCPLAY_LOG=<file> (stdout+stderr into a file; "-" = never; unset = automatic when there is no console)
//   sound: MCPLAY_SOUNDS=<dir with bank.json + wavs> (default: <exe dir>/sounds, then $HOME/.cache/mcplay/sounds; made by tools/sounds/gen tools/sounds/mc.json <dir>)
//          FIRN_AUDIO=file:/x.wav|null|device (default device); MCPLAY_AUDIO=0 off; MCPLAY_VOL_<MASTER|BLOCKS|AMBIENT|PLAYERS|HOSTILE|NEUTRAL|MUSIC|UI>=0..100; M = mute
//   packs: MC_PACKS / MC_PACK_CONFIG / MC_PACK_AUTO (see docs/mc/resourcepacks.md); Ctrl+F5 = hot reload (F5 = camera first / third back / third front) (atlas + pack sounds), animated tiles tick at 20 Hz
//          MC_PACK_SOUNDS=synth|original|both (default synth; original/both read sounds.json + OGG of the packs, both = synth bank + pack events on top)
//          config file (MC_PACK_CONFIG) line `sounds=synth|original|both` does the same; O = switch pack sounds off/on while playing; pack "weight" entries are honoured
//   MCPLAY_DIG_MS=700  hold time before the "finish digging" packet in survival (there is no hardness table yet)
//   MCPLAY_PLACE_ID=0  block state id painted locally on a place click (0 = wait for the server's Block Update)
//   MCPLAY_ENTITIES=0  do not draw entity boxes (spawn / move / destroy packets are still tracked; end line `mcplay: entities ...`)
//   MCPLAY_PROGRESS=1  every 10 sim ticks one `progress` line (ticks, pos, chunks, ground, y, walked_mm, steps): tests wait on SIM time, not wall time
//   MCPLAY_QUIT_FILE=<path>  quit as soon as that file exists (tests: end when the scripted actions are done, however slow the box is)
//   MCPLAY_RUN_S=0     quit after N seconds (tests)       MCPLAY_SHOT=<file.png>  write the last frame as PNG on exit + print its hash
//   MCPLAY_AUDIO=0     sound: 0 off, 1 on (FIRN_AUDIO=null|file:<path>|device selects the sink)
//
// Frame order: pump events -> network (chunks, block updates) -> 20 Hz ticks (movement, position packets) -> pick -> mouse actions ->
// clear, sky, world, light tint, selection box, HUD -> present. Packets are applied as they arrive: Block Update / Multi Block
// Change change the world (mc_blockset) and dirty the mesh cache (wr_mark_block).
